[0.000, "o", "ary).\r\n\u001b[K\n  We'll set up the interactive course inside \u001b[94m./tutorial/\u001b[m so the root project stays untouched. Before I draft\r\n  \u001b[94mtutorial/MISSION.md\u001b[m and the first lesson, let's clarify your goal one step at a time:\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1mWhat does success look like for you at the end of this course?\u001b[m For example:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mRebuild & master this app from the ground up\u001b[m — progressively reconstructing the Parts Tracker in \u001b[94m.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94m/tutorial/apps/\u001b[m (from Dart data models and Riverpod state up to the full workbench UI and widget tests) so you can\r\n  build new Flutter apps with the same stack.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mRead, modify, and extend this specific codebase\u001b[m — learning enough Flutter, Dart, and Riverpod through targeted\r\n  slices of this repo to confidently ship new features or changes to it.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mSomething else\u001b[m (e.g., evaluating Flutter vs. React/React Native for an upcoming project)?\r\n\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[90m? for shortcuts\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[13D\u001b[?2026l"]
