[0.000, "o", "m## Implications\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m6 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m- Anchor every new Dart/Flutter concept to its closest React/TypeScript counterpart—and explicitly call out\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mwhere the analogy breaks (e.g., Dart's nominal typing vs TypeScript's structural typing, compile-time \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`const`\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mwidget canonicalization vs \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`React.memo`\u001b[39m, and Riverpod's \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`AsyncNotifier`\u001b[39m outside the widget tree vs React hooks\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mbound to component instances).\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m7 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m- Introduce Dart syntax (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`const`\u001b[39m, named parameters \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`{required ...}`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`super.key`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`part`\u001b[39m directives, mixins\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`with`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Future<T>`\u001b[39m) inline as eac"]
